Offline registration and schema gates:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python -m py_compile unreal_mcp_server.py tools\chaos_tools.py scripts\smoke_chaos_destruction_learning.py scripts\smoke_chaos_destruction_learning_live.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\smoke_tool_registration.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\test_chaos_tools_response_schema.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\test_tool_policy_contract.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\test_tool_discovery_contract.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\run_response_schema_tests.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\python_tool_response_schema_audit.py check
```

Native compile and editor automation gate (strict raw JSON, exact optimistic
types, no-op dirty suppression, and Solver Undo/Redo resync registration):

```powershell
$Project = (Resolve-Path .\MCPGameProject\MCPGameProject.uproject).ProviderPath
& 'C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6\Engine\Build\BatchFiles\Build.bat' MCPGameProjectEditor Win64 Development -Project="$Project" -WaitMutex
& 'C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6\Engine\Binaries\Win64\UnrealEditor-Cmd.exe' $Project `
  -unattended -nop4 -nosplash -NullRHI `
  '-ExecCmds=Automation RunTests UnrealMCP.Chaos.StrictNativeJson;Quit' `
  '-TestExit=Automation Test Queue Empty'
```

Actual MRQ execution is deliberately separate from the read-only inspector.
It requires a new output root so stale files cannot satisfy the gate, renders
frames 0-59 at 640x360 plus frame 30 again, decodes every PNG, rejects
zero-byte/black/wrong-size output, and writes per-frame SHA-256 plus a
perceptual repeat check:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\run_chaos_cinematic_mrq.py `
  --sequence-path /Game/_MCP_Temp/ChaosDestructionLearning/Cinematic/S05/LS_S05_MultiShot `
  --map-path /Game/_MCP_Temp/ChaosDestructionLearning/Cinematic/S05/L_S05_MultiShot `
  --output-root .\Python\output\chaos_cinematic\mrq_run_01 `
  --manifest .\Python\output\chaos_cinematic\mrq_run_01.json `
  --chaos-state-sha256 <64-hex-observed-state-hash> --port 55562
```

The five sample shells are authored only in an isolated editor and refuse to
replace existing assets. Record real caches before running the separate bind
phase:

```powershell
$env:UNREAL_MCP_CHAOS_CINEMATIC_MUTATION = "1"
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\author_chaos_cinematic_samples.py `
  --phase author --evidence .\Python\output\chaos_cinematic\author.json --port 55562
# Run the live record suite here.
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\author_chaos_cinematic_samples.py `
  --phase bind --evidence .\Python\output\chaos_cinematic\bind.json --port 55562
```

Read-only live surface smoke (does not create assets or control editor lifecycle):

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\smoke_chaos_destruction_learning.py
```

Exit code `2` means the bridge is unavailable, does not have the current command surface loaded, or has no authored fixture.

Opt-in isolated-editor mutation and map-lifecycle regression:

```powershell
$env:UNREAL_MCP_CHAOS_LIVE_MUTATION = "1"
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\smoke_chaos_destruction_learning_live.py
```

The live runner uses `safe_new_preview_map`, configures only the exact current learning level, saves it, switches to a second native preview map, then opens the learning map and switches away again. Run it only against an isolated bridge; it intentionally changes the current map and temp assets.
